class:: PipeWire
summary:: Query and edit the PipeWire graph from sclang (via pw-link)
categories:: External Control>PipeWire
related:: Classes/PipeWirePatch, Classes/PipeWirePort, Classes/PipeWireLink

description::

Class-side access to the PipeWire graph: list nodes, ports and links, and
create/destroy links between ports. It is a thin, pure-sclang wrapper around the
emphasis::pw-link:: command-line tool, called through
link::Classes/String#-unixCmdGetStdOut:: (blocking, so operations happen in
order). No C++ primitives are needed — the PipeWire graph is managed
out-of-process, so any client may rewire it.

For a server-oriented interface (route a specific link::Classes/Server::'s
client), see link::Classes/PipeWirePatch::.

subsection:: Requirements

code::pw-link:: must be on PATH (from the emphasis::pipewire:: /
emphasis::pipewire-utils:: package).

ClassMethods::

private:: prCmdString, prRun, prSystem, prQuote, prParsePorts, prIsLinkLine, prSplitPort, prPortNumber, prSortPorts, prCutToken, prTrim, prIsWS

method:: program
Get/set the command used (default code::"pw-link"::).

method:: remoteName
Get/set the PipeWire remote daemon name (passed as code::--remote=NAME::).
code::nil:: (default) uses the default daemon. Use this to address a second
PipeWire daemon.

subsection:: Queries

method:: outPorts
method:: inPorts
All output / input ports on the graph.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWirePort::.

method:: ports
code::outPorts ++ inPorts::.

method:: nodes
The distinct node names on the graph, sorted.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/String::.

method:: portsOf
All ports (both directions) belonging to a node.
argument:: nodeName
The code::node.name:: string.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWirePort::.

method:: outPortsOf
method:: inPortsOf
A node's output / input ports in strong::channel order:: (index 0 = first
channel). code::.size:: is the channel count — use these to index and count any
client's ports.
argument:: nodeName
The code::node.name:: string.
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWirePort::.

method:: links
All links on the graph (deduplicated, each with a stable id).
returns:: an Array of link::Classes/PipeWireLink::.

method:: report
Post a readable summary of nodes (with out/in port counts) and links.

subsection:: Operations

All operations block until pw-link returns, and post a warning on failure.

method:: connect
Create a link from one output port to one input port.
argument:: outName
The full code::"node:port":: name of the output port (e.g. from
link::Classes/PipeWirePort#-fullName::).
argument:: inName
The full code::"node:port":: name of the input port.
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

method:: disconnect
Remove the link between a specific output and input port.
argument:: outName
argument:: inName
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

method:: disconnectLink
Remove a link by its id.
argument:: linkId
The link id (see link::Classes/PipeWireLink#-id::).
returns:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

Examples::

code::
PipeWire.report;                 // whole graph
PipeWire.nodes;                  // node names

// How many channels does a node have?
PipeWire.outPortsOf("alsa_input.usb-...pro-input-0").size;

// A specific port object:
~p = PipeWire.outPorts.detect { |x| x.node.contains("pro-input") };
~p.fullName;

// Low-level connect / disconnect (full port names):
PipeWire.connect("scMain playback:output_AUX0",
    "alsa_output.usb-...pro-output-0:playback_AUX0");

// Remove by id:
PipeWire.links.do { |lk| lk.postln };
PipeWire.disconnectLink(113);

// Address a second PipeWire daemon:
PipeWire.remoteName = "my-remote";
PipeWire.nodes;
PipeWire.remoteName = nil;
::
